# RFC #362 desktop.14 · A1 (Windows distribution patch, also valid upstream):
# simple / advanced working mode.
#
#  * Simple mode puts the AI conversation in the centre of the canvas workspace
#    and dims the canvas behind it (the canvas stays mounted, so running work and
#    selections are untouched). Advanced is the unchanged canvas workflow.
#  * The choice is a local preference (opendirector.work-mode.v1), toggled from
#    the top bar. Switching never edits a project and never cancels a reply:
#    verified by verification/work_mode.mjs (a reply started in simple mode
#    completes after switching to advanced; the preference survives a reload).
#  * First run (A2): a non-modal picker appears once, after the model-setup
#    welcome is dismissed and only while no mode has been chosen. Either
#    choice is saved and changeable from the top bar.
#  * Simple mode presets (A1): a drawer above the composer offers four system
#    presets that fill the draft (editable there) and a reference-image button
#    that reuses the composer's existing file input.
#  * Scope: result cards are follow-up work.
#
